 122:Drivers/STM32C0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32c0xx_hal.c **** /**
 123:Drivers/STM32C0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32c0xx_hal.c ****   * @brief  Configure the Flash prefetch and the Instruction cache,
 124:Drivers/STM32C0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32c0xx_hal.c ****   *         the time base source, NVIC and any required global low level hardware
 125:Drivers/STM32C0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32c0xx_hal.c ****   *         by calling the HAL_MspInit() callback function to be optionally defined in user file
 126:Drivers/STM32C0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32c0xx_hal.c ****   *         stm32c0xx_hal_msp.c.
 127:Drivers/STM32C0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32c0xx_hal.c ****   *
 128:Drivers/STM32C0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32c0xx_hal.c ****   * @note   HAL_Init() function is called at the beginning of program after reset and before
 129:Drivers/STM32C0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32c0xx_hal.c ****   *         the clock configuration.
 130:Drivers/STM32C0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32c0xx_hal.c ****   *
 131:Drivers/STM32C0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32c0xx_hal.c ****   * @note   In the default implementation the System Timer (Systick) is used as source of time base
 132:Drivers/STM32C0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32c0xx_hal.c ****   *         The Systick configuration is based on HSI clock, as HSI is the clock
 133:Drivers/STM32C0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32c0xx_hal.c ****   *         used after a system Reset.
 134:Drivers/STM32C0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32c0xx_hal.c ****   *         Once done, time base tick starts incrementing: the tick variable counter is incremented
 135:Drivers/STM32C0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32c0xx_hal.c ****   *         each 1ms in the SysTick_Handler() interrupt handler.
 136:Drivers/STM32C0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32c0xx_hal.c ****   *
 137:Drivers/STM32C0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32c0xx_hal.c ****   * @retval HAL status
 138:Drivers/STM32C0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32c0xx_hal.c ****   */
